From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:38:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Many motes to a cell, each its own size, opacity and
 brightness

Patch 0038 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user's test of the dust, 2026-10-08, at the Temple of Time's window with Bright and Thick: "this
is bright and thick which shows almost no particles. so the brightness setting is fine! it works
well, BUT the density is WAY too low. this thick setting should probably be a new "very sparse"
setting and then it needs to densen significantly as it goes through each". And: "there needs to
be variance in size, there needs to be variance in opacity, and there needs to be a variance in
brightness for every single particle ... most of them, would be more transparent ... the particle
size would then control ... the median size".

A density is now motes to a cell, from 0 to 8: the whole part in every cell and the fraction by
chance, where it was a share of cells holding one mote. Each mote draws its own place, its own
radius (half to twice the place's median, from two new values in tuneAmbience, y indoors and z
outdoors, held between three quarters of a pixel and eight pixels across), its own opacity (from
0.12 to 1, most of them near the faint end) and its own brightness (a third either side of the
place's visibility). The visibility stays the overall level.

